6
00:00:18,266 --> 00:00:22,222
Put those options on the screen first,
then reveal the measurements.

7
00:00:22,402 --> 00:00:25,614
This helps stakeholders discuss the same
decision.

8
00:00:27,090 --> 00:00:31,123
The median wait was thirteen hours against
a target of fourteen.

9
00:00:31,303 --> 00:00:36,018
Active review effort was twenty-six
minutes against a limit of twenty-seven.

10
00:00:36,198 --> 00:00:40,581
Cost was two hundred and forty dollars
against a three hundred dollar cap.

11
00:00:40,761 --> 00:00:45,071
Rework was seventeen and a half percent
against a fifteen percent ceiling.

12
00:00:45,251 --> 00:00:50,487
One post-merge defect appeared in each
window, and the pilot recorded zero

13
00:00:50,487 --> 00:00:52,822
serious data or access incidents.

14
00:00:54,298 --> 00:00:57,988
Return to the seven requests that needed
material rework.

15
00:00:58,168 --> 00:01:02,574
Four touched extra files, which the
reviewers identified from the diff.

16
00:01:02,754 --> 00:01:07,665
The manager asks the tech lead to test a
tighter scope instruction and an author

17
00:01:07,665 --> 00:01:09,814
diff checkpoint before publication.

18
00:01:09,994 --> 00:01:14,367
A reviewer still makes the independent
decision on each pull request.

19
00:01:14,547 --> 00:01:19,576
The follow-up evidence will show whether
those two changes address the recurring

20
00:01:19,576 --> 00:01:20,520
review concern.

21
00:01:21,965 --> 00:01:26,328
The follow-up keeps the same service,
tools, and eligibility rules.

22
00:01:26,508 --> 00:01:31,079
For the next four weeks, the engineering
lead updates the author workflow and

23
00:01:31,079 --> 00:01:33,216
checks the rework reasons each week.

24
00:01:33,396 --> 00:01:38,387
Use the same measurement definitions and
keep a record of other process changes.

25
00:01:38,567 --> 00:01:43,571
With another comparable sample of forty,
six rework cases would meet the fifteen

26
00:01:43,571 --> 00:01:44,572
percent ceiling.

27
00:01:44,752 --> 00:01:48,573
Report the actual sample size alongside
the rework rate.

28
00:01:50,048 --> 00:01:55,103
If the benefit and all guardrails hold,
propose expansion to one comparable team

29
00:01:55,103 --> 00:01:57,631
and document what it must have in place.

30
00:01:57,811 --> 00:02:02,467
If there is still a well-understood,
correctable issue, decide whether a

31
00:02:02,467 --> 00:02:05,054
further focused adjustment is justified.

32
00:02:05,234 --> 00:02:10,419
If a serious data or access problem
occurs, pause agent use in scope and

33
00:02:10,419 --> 00:02:13,084
follow the existing incident process.

34
00:02:13,264 --> 00:02:17,404
The decision record should make the
evidence and owner easy to find.

35
00:02:18,882 --> 00:02:23,669
The decision is to adjust this pilot by
narrowing file scope and adding a diff

36
00:02:23,669 --> 00:02:24,344
checkpoint.

37
00:02:24,524 --> 00:02:29,490
The written rationale includes the shorter
wait, the rework miss, the sample behind

38
00:02:29,490 --> 00:02:32,362
